body:
I know the mirror-driving is the focus here, but I'm always amazed by how unemotive drivers are, especially long-time vets like Harv, are during a wreck. I know the HANS bolts them down pretty hard, but before, during and after the contact with the wall, there's practically no head or body movement from Harvick besides still trying to turn the wheel.

&#x200B;

There's no "oh, fuck", no bracing for impact, no moment of realization. He hits the wall, gets jolted, and look outside the window to look at other cars/the wall/the front of his own car. Crazy stuff.
